From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Leiter <8675906+MaxLeiter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:37:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Async functions and await

async function declarations and expressions, async arrow functions, and
async methods in object literals and classes. await is valid in their
bodies; elsewhere, including at the top level of a script, it is a
SyntaxError. Async generators and for await are not supported.

An async function compiles as a generator that yields what it awaits.
Calling it starts the generator, and NativePromise steps it: each
awaited value is resolved as Promise.resolve would, and the generator
resumes from a reaction job once it settles, with no derived promise in
between, which gives the job ordering of the spec. A throw, or an
awaited rejection that is not caught, rejects the function's promise.

Compiled generators cannot yet keep a call in progress across a yield,
which an await inside call arguments needs, so the compiler leaves
scripts that contain async functions to the interpreter.

Microtasks now count towards the instruction observer, so that an async
function that only awaits cannot run unobserved.

